1. CREATE DATABASE

	CREATE DATABASE [IF NOT EXISTS] database_name
	-- [CHARACTER SET charset_name]
	-- [COLLATE collation_name]

2. TO LIST OUT ALL THE AVAILABL DATABASES - show databases;
	
	mysql - is the system database that contains tables that store information required by the MySQL server
	information_schema - provides access to database metadata
	performance_schema - is a feature for monitoring MySQL Server execution at a low level
	sys - a set of objects that helps DBAs and developers interpret data collected by the Performance Schema

3. To return the database which we're currently working w/ & if you don't choose any database, 
	it will give NULL as a result. select database();
	
4. To switch to particular database - use database_name;

5. To drop database: - This will delete the currently chosen database with all of its tables permanently.
	Syntax: drop database database_name;
	Example: drop database student; [OR] drop database if exists student;
	
Note: In MySQL, schema is  a synonym for database. so wherever we have the word database or databases, 
we can use schema or schemas.

6. Rename a database

GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON new_database.* TO 'username'@'localhost';